Don't clamp spdif passthrough to the AudioTrack native output rate

ao_audiotrack clamps every format to AudioTrack.getNativeOutputSampleRate,
spdif included. E-AC-3, DTS-HD and TrueHD are carried as IEC 61937 at
192000 Hz, above the native (mixer) rate AudioTrack reports (48000 Hz on
the p6), so the AO opens at the native rate and player/audio.c rejects
it:

    requested format: 192000 Hz, stereo channels, spdif-eac3
    AudioTrack.nativeOutputSampleRate = 48000
    Passthrough format unsupported.

and mpv falls back to PCM. Those codecs were therefore never passed
through on Android, whatever audio-spdif said; any spdif format whose
rate exceeds the native rate is refused the same way (48000 Hz AC-3 on a
44100 Hz device, for instance).

Skip the clamp for spdif formats. The rate of an IEC 61937 stream is set
by the codec, not the mixer; if the device can't open it, AudioTrack
creation fails and mpv falls back to PCM exactly as before.

With the rate no longer rejected, the high bitrate formats (TrueHD,
DTS-HD MA: 8 channels at 192000 Hz) would reach AudioTrack as a stereo
track, which consumes a quarter of their byte rate. Open those with the
7.1 mask. The Java API accepts a 7.1 IEC 61937 track since API 31 (S)
and throws before that; either a throw or a HAL without an 8-channel
IEC 61937 profile fails init, and mpv falls back to PCM.

diff --git a/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c b/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
index f483ccc8e8..c8b936b8fe 100644
--- a/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
@@ -673,7 +673,13 @@ static int init(struct ao *ao)
         p->format = AudioFormat.ENCODING_PCM_16BIT;
     }
 
-    if (AudioTrack.getNativeOutputSampleRate) {
+    // The native output rate describes the PCM mixer, not the HDMI link.
+    // IEC 61937 is an exact bitstream whose rate is dictated by the codec
+    // (192000 Hz for E-AC-3, DTS-HD and TrueHD), so clamping it only makes
+    // player/audio.c reject the AO ("Passthrough format unsupported.") and
+    // fall back to PCM. If the device can't open the requested rate,
+    // AudioTrack creation fails below, which falls back the same way.
+    if (AudioTrack.getNativeOutputSampleRate && !af_fmt_is_spdif(ao->format)) {
         jint samplerate = MP_JNI_CALL_STATIC_INT(
             AudioTrack.clazz,
             AudioTrack.getNativeOutputSampleRate,
@@ -711,7 +717,18 @@ static int init(struct ao *ao)
     };
     static_assert(MP_ARRAY_SIZE(layout_map) == MP_ARRAY_SIZE(layouts), "");
     if (p->format == AudioFormat.ENCODING_IEC61937) {
-        p->channel_config = AudioFormat.CHANNEL_OUT_STEREO;
+        // High bitrate formats (TrueHD, DTS-HD MA) are carried as 8 channels
+        // at 192000 Hz. A stereo track would consume them at a quarter of
+        // their byte rate; Android accepts a 7.1 IEC 61937 track since API 31
+        // and refuses one before that, which fails init and falls back.
+        if (ao->channels.num == 8 && AudioFormat.CHANNEL_OUT_7POINT1_SURROUND) {
+            p->channel_config = AudioFormat.CHANNEL_OUT_7POINT1_SURROUND;
+        } else if (ao->channels.num == 2) {
+            p->channel_config = AudioFormat.CHANNEL_OUT_STEREO;
+        } else {
+            MP_ERR(ao, "unsupported spdif channel count: %d\n", ao->channels.num);
+            goto error;
+        }
     } else {
         struct mp_chmap_sel sel = {0};
         for (int i = 0; i < MP_ARRAY_SIZE(layouts); i++) {
